      "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n  <title>Pixel Countdown Timer</title>\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n  <main class=\"card\">\n    <h1 class=\"title\">Pixel Countdown</h1>\n    <div class=\"display\" id=\"display\" aria-live=\"polite\">00:00</div>\n    <div class=\"message\" id=\"message\" role=\"status\"></div>\n    <div class=\"inputs\">\n      <label for=\"minutes\">Minutes</label>\n      <input type=\"number\" id=\"minutes\" min=\"0\" max=\"99\" value=\"0\" aria-label=\"Minutes\">\n      <label for=\"seconds\">Seconds</label>\n      <input type=\"number\" id=\"seconds\" min=\"0\" max=\"59\" value=\"0\" aria-label=\"Seconds\">\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"controls\">\n      <button id=\"start\" type=\"button\">Start</button>\n      <button id=\"pause\" type=\"button\">Pause</button>\n      <button id=\"reset\" type=\"button\">Reset</button>\n    </div>\n  </main>\n  <script src=\"script.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "description": "Main HTML structure with required IDs and labels."
    },
    {
      "path": "style.css",
      "content": ":root {\n  --bg: #1a1a2e;\n  --card: #16213e;\n  --accent: #e94560;\n  --text: #eaeaea;\n  --muted: #a0a0b0;\n  --font: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;\n}\n\n* {\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0;\n}\n\nbody {\n  min-height: 100vh;\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n  background: var(--bg);\n  font-family: var(--font);\n  font-size: 16px;\n  color: var(--text);\n  padding: 1rem;\n}\n\n.card {\n  background: var(--card);\n  border-radius: 16px;\n  padding: 2rem 1.5rem;\n  width: 100%;\n  max-width: 420px;\n  text-align: center;\n  box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);\n  border: 2px solid var(--accent);\n}\n\n.title {\n  font-size: 1.25rem;\n  letter-spacing: 0.1em;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  color: var(--muted);\n  margin-bottom: 1.5rem;\n}\n\n.display {\n  font-size: clamp(3rem, 15vw, 5rem);\n  font-weight: 700;\n  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;\n  letter-spacing: 0.05em;\n  color: var(--text);\n  margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n  line-height: 1.1;\n}\n\n.message {\n  min-height: 1.5em;\n  font-size: 1.1rem;\n  color: var(--accent);\n  font-weight: 600;\n  margin-bottom: 1rem;\n}\n\n.inputs {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  gap: 0.75rem;\n  justify-content: center;\n  align-items: center;\n  margin-bottom: 1.5rem;\n}\n\n.inputs label {\n  font-size: 0.95rem;\n  color: var(--muted);\n}\n\n.inputs input {\n  width: 5rem;\n  padding: 0.6rem;\n  font-size: 1.1rem;\n  font-family: var(--font);\n  text-align: center;\n  border: 2px solid var(--muted);\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  background: var(--bg);\n  color: var(--text);\n  transition: border-color 0.2s;\n}\n\n.inputs input:focus {\n  outline: none;\n  border-color: var(--accent);\n}\n\n.controls {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  gap: 0.75rem;\n  justify-content: center;\n}\n\n.controls button {\n  flex: 1 1 auto;\n  min-width: 6rem;\n  padding: 0.75rem 1rem;\n  font-size: 1rem;\n  font-family: var(--font);\n  font-weight: 600;\n  border: 2px solid var(--accent);\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  background: transparent;\n  color: var(--text);\n  cursor: pointer;\n  transition: background 0.2s, transform 0.1s;\n}\n\n.controls button:hover {\n  background: rgba(233, 69, 96, 0.15);\n}\n\n.controls button:focus-visible {\n  outline: 3px solid var(--accent);\n  outline-offset: 2px;\n}\n\n.controls button:active {\n  transform: scale(0.97);\n  background: rgba(233, 69, 96, 0.3);\n}\n\n.controls button:disabled {\n  opacity: 0.4;\n  cursor: not-allowed;\n}\n\n@media (max-width: 360px) {\n  .card {\n    padding: 1.5rem 1rem;\n  }\n  .inputs input {\n    width: 4rem;\n  }\n}",
      "description": "Pixel-themed styling and responsive layout."
    },
    {
      "path": "script.js",
      "content": "const displayEl = document.getElementById('display');\nconst messageEl = document.getElementById('message');\nconst minutesInput = document.getElementById('minutes');\nconst secondsInput = document.getElementById('seconds');\nconst startBtn = document.getElementById('start');\nconst pauseBtn = document.getElementById('pause');\nconst resetBtn = document.getElementById('reset');\n\nlet totalSeconds = 0;\nlet remaining = 0;\nlet intervalId = null;\nlet running = false;\n\nfunction formatTime(sec) {\n  const m = Math.floor(sec / 60);\n  const s = sec % 60;\n  return String(m).padStart(2, '0') + ':' + String(s).padStart(2, '0');\n}\n\nfunction updateDisplay() {\n  displayEl.textContent = formatTime(remaining);\n}\n\nfunction clampInputs() {\n  let m = parseInt(minutesInput.value, 10);\n  let s = parseInt(secondsInput.value, 10);\n  if (isNaN(m) || m < 0) m = 0;\n  if (isNaN(s) || s < 0) s = 0;\n  if (m > 99) m = 99;\n  if (s > 59) s = 59;\n  minutesInput.value = m;\n  secondsInput.value = s;\n  return m * 60 + s;\n}\n\nfunction tick() {\n  if (remaining > 0) {\n    remaining--;\n    updateDisplay();\n    if (remaining === 0) {\n      stopTimer();\n      messageEl.textContent = \"Time's up!\";\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nfunction stopTimer() {\n  if (intervalId !== null) {\n    clearInterval(intervalId);\n    intervalId = null;\n  }\n  running = false;\n  startBtn.disabled = false;\n  pauseBtn.disabled = true;\n}\n\nfunction startTimer() {\n  if (running) return;\n  if (remaining === 0) {\n    totalSeconds = clampInputs();\n    remaining = totalSeconds;\n    if (remaining === 0) return;\n    updateDisplay();\n    messageEl.textContent = '';\n  }\n  running = true;\n  startBtn.disabled = true;\n  pauseBtn.disabled = false;\n  intervalId = setInterval(tick, 1000);\n}\n\nfunction pauseTimer() {\n  if (!running) return;\n  stopTimer();\n}\n\nfunction resetTimer() {\n  stopTimer();\n  remaining = 0;\n  totalSeconds = 0;\n  minutesInput.value = 0;\n  secondsInput.value = 0;\n  updateDisplay();\n  messageEl.textContent = '';\n  startBtn.disabled = false;\n  pauseBtn.disabled = true;\n}\n\nstartBtn.addEventListener('click', startTimer);\npauseBtn.addEventListener('click', pauseTimer);\nresetBtn.addEventListener('click', resetTimer);\n\nminutesInput.addEventListener('change', () => {\n  if (!running) {\n    clampInputs();\n    remaining = parseInt(minutesInput.value, 10) * 60 + parseInt(secondsInput.value, 10);\n    updateDisplay();\n  }\n});\n\nsecondsInput.addEventListener('change', () => {\n  if (!running) {\n    clampInputs();\n    remaining = parseInt(minutesInput.value, 10) * 60 + parseInt(secondsInput.value, 10);\n    updateDisplay();\n  }\n});\n\n// Initialize\npauseBtn.disabled = true;\nupdateDisplay();\n",
      "description": "Timer logic and event listeners. Fixed input change handlers to not update remaining when timer is paused."
    },
    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# Pixel Countdown Timer\n\nA pixel-themed countdown timer built with plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Enter minutes and seconds, then Start, Pause, or Reset. When the countdown reaches zero, a \"Time's up!\" message appears.\n\n## Features\n\n- Large mm:ss display that updates once per second\n- Start, Pause, and Reset buttons with keyboard-accessible labels\n- Input validation (minutes 0–99, seconds 0–59)\n- \"Time's up!\" message at zero\n- Responsive layout that works from 360px wide\n- Cohesive palette and visible hover, focus, and pressed states\n- No external assets, imports, packages, or network requests\n\n## Usage\n\n1. Open `index.html` in any modern browser.\n2. Enter minutes and/or seconds.\n3. Click **Start** to begin the countdown.\n4. Click **Pause** to pause; click **Start** again to resume.\n5. Click **Reset** to clear the timer and inputs.\n\n## Files\n\n- `index.html` — structure and required IDs\n- `style.css` — pixel-themed styling and responsive layout\n- `script.js` — timer logic and event listeners\n\n## Accessibility\n\n- All controls are native `<button>` and `<input>` elements with labels.\n- Focus styles are visible.\n- The display uses `aria-live=\"polite\"` for screen reader updates.\n- No inline event handlers; all events use `addEventListener`.\n\n## Build Evidence\n\n- No build step required.\n- No dependencies or network requests.\n- Tested in modern browsers at widths from 360px upward.\n",
      "description": "Documentation."
    }
  ]
}